{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WAVE 2 Q2 - CONVERGENCE, corrected. A MEASUREMENT DEFECT was found and fixed mid-analysis: floored findings retain decision=='advisory', not 'dropped' - of 1,191 findings with a non-null drop_reason, ZERO carry decision=='dropped'. The first pass tested only decision=='dropped' and so counted every floor drop as shown to the author. Corrected test is decision=='dropped' OR drop_reason is not None. Corrected results on 399 tickets with >=3 reviews (2,711 plan reviews across 778 tickets): THE TWO AXES DISAGREE. Verdict converges - blocking findings 2.04->1.50->1.15, 41.6% of tickets monotone, 96.2% end at zero blocking. Author-visible text does NOT - 7.54, 7.30, 6.96, 7.21, 7.74, 7.69, 8.59, 8.20, 7.23, 8.21 across rounds 1-10, a shallow dip then a rise past the start; 20.3% monotone, 5.8% end at zero. The driver is NOVELTY, not resurrection: 69.6% of what an author sees in round N was never shown before, and on BYTE-IDENTICAL material (unchanged fingerprint) it is still 57.1% - a nondeterminism floor. Resurrection is 0.4% and block->floored is 0.0% in every segment. The floor fires on 20.4% of rounds and removes 6.6% of findings overall, 15.6% on eligible transitions vs 0.8% on ineligible. drop_reason breakdown: 1,088 novelty, 23 completion, 20 drift, 0 duplicate - so the floor is NOT what would address the +49 duplication problem. Era segmentation is moot: 99.5% of reviews postdate the 2026-07-15 BLOCK-loop fix."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789000936152338001,"uuid":"dd2c74ad-6cb8-4c1e-bdef-381fd0c4b5d4"}